r","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-18T18:27:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T18:27:36Z","body":"**δ review REV-T4B-2026-10-19-ce568ce** — verdict: **APPROVE**\n\nScope: full diff of #45 at `ce568ce98d0f7f3abff1c6faf8eb0c55d68715e9` (5 files, +426/−1: `tools/spikes/db-invariant/bench/drift-gate.sh`, `bench/drift-fixtures/rename-unused-column.sh`, `bench/drift-fixtures/stale-after-sql-change.sh`, one `bench:drift-gate` script line in `tools/spikes/db-invariant/package.json`, and the new A5 section in `docs/plans/2026-10-17-spike-a-report.md`). Reviewer role: agent. Accountable sponsor: the maintainer. The generator ran on automatic model routing, so its family is not pinned. The maintainer reviewed this receipt and authorized the merge.\n\nBlocking: none.\n\nVerified at `ce568ce`:\n- Scope matches the T4b file list exactly. The package.json edit is the single additive `bench:drift-gate` line the plan names (β-M5). The report file uses the real run date (2026-10-17), as T6 requires, and holds only the A5 skeleton section. `measure.mjs`, the generators, the corpus, the committed artifacts, `.github/workflows/` and `scripts/gates/` are unchanged, and `scripts/gates/approvals/maintainer.pub` is untouched.\n- The drift gate fails closed. It runs under `set -euo pipefail` and validates host, port, user and band. It refuses to run if the interface's worktree or index already differs from HEAD. For each band it drops and recreates `spike_bench_<N>`, applies the committed `schema.sql` with `ON_ERROR_STOP=1`, regenerates `database-types.ts` with the pinned kysely-codegen 0.20.0 flags, and runs `git diff --exit-code HEAD` on it. A diff exits 1, and a missing tool, missing artifact, psql error, codegen failure or git error exits non-zero. No band is skipped. All four interfaces are tracked at the head. Codegen output is redacted for the password, both raw and URL-encoded.\n- Both fixtures refuse a dirty or staged tree, mutate only band-50 `schema.sql`, run the gate, require exit 1 plus the band-50 drift line and the expected `+` interface line, then restore from HEAD and re-check. An EXIT trap also restores on any failure path.\n- Raw transcripts in the PR body, from head `ce568ce`: the clean gate passes on bands 50, 75, 200 and 400. The rename fixture shows `+ opened_at` (gate exit 1). The stale-SQL fixture shows `+ drift_marker` (gate exit 1). A staged interface is refused before migrate.\n- The curve table matches bench-dispatch run 39044052211 in all 16 values. Corpus wall ms / RSS KiB, then baseline: band 50 2420/396212, 610/228384. Band 75 3410/429960, 760/236704. Band 200 18130/769568, 750/296792. Band 400 97440/1356892, 900/338320. No stress target is over the ceiling, so no §3.0 record is due. There is no ergonomics verdict: the report defers it to T6 and binds the ceiling to the band-75 acceptance point only.\n- Hygiene: the password comes only from env vars, and only loopback appears as a default. There are no machine paths, personal data, predecessor references or model identities. The three branch commits (`31071ca`, `fa38f7b`, `ce568ce`) have conventional messages, the only trailers are `AI-assisted: yes` and the maintainer's co-author line, and none has tool markers or URLs.\n- CI: 7/7 required checks are green on the head. Codex finished on `ce568ce`, and every review thread has a fix or decline reply. Codex's two open P1s are covered. 4308131990 cites `789f99e`, which is not a branch commit: it is GitHub's squash preview built from the PR body, so the merge uses a clean squash message. 4308131993 asks for this receipt.\n- Not rerun by δ: the gate and the fixtures. The evidence is the pasted transcripts from the pinned harness. The independent rerun belongs to T6.\n\nNon-blocking notes:\n- `drift-gate.sh` has no restore trap of its own. On drift or a codegen failure it leaves the regenerated `database-types.ts` in the worktree. A rerun then refuses with \"already differs from HEAD\", so the gate still fails closed. Record this in the report or restore the file on exit.\n- The gate drops `spike_bench_<N>` `WITH (FORCE)` on whatever `BENCH_PG_HOST` points to. The names are fixed and the default is the loopback harness port, which is fine for a spike tool that is not a required check.\n- The gate checks that the interface file exists, not that it is tracked in HEAD. All four are tracked today. `git cat-file -e HEAD:<path>` would close that gap.\n- Both fixtures call `mktemp` before setting the trap, so an early exit could leave one empty temp file.\n- The curve reuses the T4a dispatch, which already measured all four bands with the same workflow. Plan step 1 is met without a second dispatch.\n\nAI-assisted: yes\n","author_association":"OWNER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tachkovsa/plerni/issues/comments/6253526008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":1210556,"client_id":"Iv23liGzp2hacMWjAyXc","slug":"cursor","node_id":"A_kwHOB44z8s4AEni8","owner":{"login":"cursor","id":126759922,"node_id":"O_kgDOB44z8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126759922?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor","html_url":"https://github.com/cursor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":fa